 ## Overview
-This method optimizes a 3D volume density (extinction/scattering) stored on a regular grid to match a set of synthetic reference images [S2, S3, unofficial]. It accounts for direct and indirect illumination by using path replay backpropagation to compute derivatives of delta tracking and volumetric multiple scattering [S2, S3, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of differentiable rendering and inverse rendering, where the forward rendering operator is differentiated to propagate gradients through integration steps [44-radiance-field-optimization.md]. Unlike standard differentiable volume rendering which often relies on analytic inversion or simple reverse-mode AD on discrete steps, this approach integrates the adjoint method directly into the path tracing loop, allowing for the optimization of complex volumetric properties while maintaining differentiability through stochastic sampling events [S2, S3, unofficial].
